Yeah, I'm fine.

275
00:14:30,078 --> 00:14:32,286
But they downgraded me.

276
00:14:32,369 --> 00:14:35,106
Doc said my chrome was a death sentence.

277
00:14:35,189 --> 00:14:36,946
No shit, tell me straight.

278
00:14:37,029 --> 00:14:39,666
My sugar, what happened back then?

279
00:14:39,749 --> 00:14:41,496
You should have died, boy.

280
00:14:41,579 --> 00:14:44,536
You fucking snapped is what happened.

281
00:14:44,619 --> 00:14:49,836
If you didn't go psycho, then
Emily would still be Miguel.

282
00:14:49,918 --> 00:14:52,366
Don't touch me, Jumba.

283
00:14:52,449 --> 00:14:54,276
Hear me out.

284
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:56,866
Don't touch me, I said.

285
00:14:56,949 --> 00:15:00,016
Mickey, it ain't his fault.

286
00:15:00,099 --> 00:15:03,036
He never meant you. Let me go.

287
00:15:03,119 --> 00:15:06,426
I can't remember memories fragged.

288
00:15:06,509 --> 00:15:09,326
That day, Emily, what happened?

289
00:15:09,409 --> 00:15:11,756
You fucking killed her.

290
00:15:11,839 --> 00:15:13,146
I what?

291
00:15:13,229 --> 00:15:14,059
Why?

292
00:15:14,142 --> 00:15:18,751
Why do we have to put her in the
ground while your Kang gets to live?

293
00:15:19,039 --> 00:15:20,837
You should have died there with her.

294
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:23,636
What kind of Edge Runner are you?

295
00:15:23,719 --> 00:15:28,896
Sugar, I'm gonna bounce.

296
00:15:28,979 --> 00:15:32,176
Jim talk soon.

297
00:15:32,259 --> 00:15:35,436
Yo, King,

298
00:15:35,519 --> 00:15:42,448
got time for a chat?

299
00:15:46,609 --> 00:15:49,240
Let me guess.

300
00:15:49,389 --> 00:15:51,242
Probably don't remember me.

301
00:15:52,459 --> 00:15:53,796
Course you don't.

302
00:15:53,879 --> 00:15:56,136
The Almighty King's a big deal.

303
00:15:56,219 --> 00:15:57,739
He's hot shit!

304
00:15:58,139 --> 00:15:59,853
What's with that look?

305
00:16:01,779 --> 00:16:04,698
You Jews ever hear his real name?

306
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:07,259
Weak Kingsley.

307
00:16:07,439 --> 00:16:09,619
Sets him better, don't it?

308
00:16:09,839 --> 00:16:11,456
Crew-killing coward.

309
00:16:11,538 --> 00:16:14,547
Don't make me finish what MaxTac couldn't!

310
00:16:16,619 --> 00:16:19,416
Hey,

311
00:16:19,499 --> 00:16:22,416
I'm at

312
00:16:22,499 --> 00:16:28,779
the spot.

313
00:16:28,899 --> 00:16:30,531
It's sealed up tight.

314
00:16:31,359 --> 00:16:32,696
You sure it's here?

315
00:16:32,779 --> 00:16:35,116
Of course, amigo mío. Thereabouts.

316
00:16:35,199 --> 00:16:36,836
What does that mean?

317
00:16:36,919 --> 00:16:39,379
Just poke around, kid. Huh?

318
00:16:39,579 --> 00:16:41,698
Old fart's no use at all.

319
00:16:41,839 --> 00:16:43,040
Oh.

320
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:53,739
Oh,

321
00:16:53,959 --> 00:16:59,606
my

322
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:06,689
God.

323
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:23,739
And

324
00:17:42,379 --> 00:17:44,039
who are you?

325
00:17:46,619 --> 00:17:49,856
A kid?

326
00:17:49,939 --> 00:17:51,055
I'm sorry.

327
00:17:51,139 --> 00:17:54,159
I was just filming you.

328
00:17:54,419 --> 00:17:55,736
Okay, that's fair.

329
00:17:55,819 --> 00:18:01,216
I should have asked, but
uh, was afraid to call out.

330
00:18:01,299 --> 00:18:06,196
So you see, I'm looking for Maelstrom.

331
00:18:06,279 --> 00:18:12,555
You're still mostly Kang? Why?

332
00:18:12,639 --> 00:18:18,765
Why I don't know, never
really thought about it.

333
00:18:18,849 --> 00:18:23,736
Yeah, you prefer life as
a sack of flesh and guts?

334
00:18:23,819 --> 00:18:25,816
No wait, what are you?

335
00:18:25,899 --> 00:18:28,015
Go on, Cross.

336
00:18:28,099 --> 00:18:34,336
Okay. Shouldn't have scrolled
without asking. I'm really sorry.

337
00:18:34,419 --> 00:18:35,595
I'm really sorry.

338
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:39,966
Not after an apology, you
watched me make the jump.

339
00:18:40,049 --> 00:18:41,925
Now it's my turn to watch you.

340
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,155
No way I'd never make it. How come?

341
00:18:44,238 --> 00:18:46,966
Because I don't have
implants like yours yet.

342
00:18:47,049 --> 00:18:49,986
You walk around acting
like you don't need them.

343
00:18:50,069 --> 00:18:52,336
So prove to me you don't.

344
00:18:52,419 --> 00:18:57,416
There

345
00:18:57,499 --> 00:19:00,916
she is,

346
00:19:00,999 --> 00:19:01,995
Talia.

347
00:19:02,079 --> 00:19:04,936
How's the new stabilizer running, Talia?

348
00:19:05,019 --> 00:19:07,166
No issues, Maelstrom.

349
00:19:07,249 --> 00:19:08,706
Who's the runt?

350
00:19:08,789 --> 00:19:10,416
No, is he volcanic?

351
00:19:10,499 --> 00:19:12,505
Yeah, all I see is meat.

352
00:19:12,589 --> 00:19:16,916
Says he's here to see your friendly faces.

353
00:19:16,999 --> 00:19:20,216
Oh, that's not exactly what I meant.

354
00:19:20,299 --> 00:19:23,236
If you're here to see us, it
means you came for one reason.

355
00:19:23,319 --> 00:19:24,896
Evolution.

356
00:19:24,979 --> 00:19:26,250
Evolution.

357
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:29,336
Ah, stop struggling.

358
00:19:29,419 --> 00:19:32,096
Relax, you're gonna look sick.

359
00:19:32,179 --> 00:19:36,356
Later,

360
00:19:36,439 --> 00:19:39,606
girly.

361
00:19:39,689 --> 00:19:43,359
Put your squealing, will ya?

362
00:19:47,119 --> 00:19:54,119
I'm

363
00:19:58,879 --> 00:19:59,708
sorry.

364
00:19:59,792 --> 00:20:03,990
You made a wise choice,
coming to see us, kid.

365
00:20:04,125 --> 00:20:06,585
So spongy, so vulnerable.

366
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:09,702
Been wanting to give this baby a whirl.

367
00:20:09,785 --> 00:20:11,920
Oh, we got a new toy.

368
00:20:12,325 --> 00:20:14,670
We said no squealing.

369
00:20:15,985 --> 00:20:19,680
Now then, want anesthesia or not?

370
00:20:20,585 --> 00:20:21,662
That a no?

371
00:20:21,745 --> 00:20:24,402
So brave. A kid.

372
00:20:24,485 --> 00:20:25,785
Whatever you say.

373
00:20:26,345 --> 00:20:27,595
Showtime.

374
00:20:28,205 --> 00:20:29,035
Huh?

375
00:20:29,125 --> 00:20:36,125
Rats.

376
00:20:36,225 --> 00:20:38,142
Plants up in dust.

377
00:20:38,225 --> 00:20:40,702
And he's not here.

378
00:20:40,785 --> 00:20:42,660
Sunshine, you alright?

379
00:20:51,065 --> 00:20:52,545
Call that a hack.

380
00:20:52,645 --> 00:20:59,062
Hey, get out of here on your own.

381
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:00,902
Not sick yet, twice.

382
00:21:01,090 --> 00:21:07,762
No.

383
00:21:07,845 --> 00:21:10,902
Fella's name is Helio.

384
00:21:10,985 --> 00:21:12,342
But you already knew that.

385
00:21:12,425 --> 00:21:14,102
By telling me where he is.

386
00:21:14,185 --> 00:21:17,242
Or you're looking to spit bullets.

387
00:21:17,325 --> 00:21:19,240
Helio ain't even in the gang no more.

388
00:21:19,405 --> 00:21:23,245
No, that wasn't what I asked.

389
00:21:25,308 --> 00:21:26,212
Okay, okay.

390
00:21:26,295 --> 00:21:28,595
I'm sure you've already told them.

391
00:21:29,565 --> 00:21:30,815
Cool.

392
00:21:40,945 --> 00:21:43,005
Oh, my camera!

393
00:21:44,305 --> 00:21:47,145
At least I brought a backup.

394
00:21:48,585 --> 00:21:50,195
Oh, hey, Chu.

395
00:21:52,305 --> 00:21:54,690
I was worried you'd leave through
the front, and I missed you.

396
00:21:54,825 --> 00:21:55,655
You brain-dead!

397
00:21:55,738 --> 00:21:58,062
You realize you could have been
sliced and diced, hack and slash,

398
00:21:58,145 --> 00:22:00,762
salt and smelt, and turned
into a toaster or worse?

399
00:22:00,845 --> 00:22:03,570
Well, I appreciate you saving me is all.

400
00:22:03,725 --> 00:22:06,700
And I want to, you know,
show you my thanks.

401
00:22:07,265 --> 00:22:08,382
Your thanks?

402
00:22:08,465 --> 00:22:10,944
Happen to live just down the block.

403
00:22:12,905 --> 00:22:14,265
Me more beer.

404
00:22:14,745 --> 00:22:16,205
There is no more.

405
00:22:16,665 --> 00:22:17,495
Huh?

406
00:22:17,578 --> 00:22:18,502
That's the last of it.

407
00:22:18,585 --> 00:22:21,460
That was all the beer we had in the house.

408
00:22:21,685 --> 00:22:22,922
No more thanks.

409
00:22:23,005 --> 00:22:26,365
I'll, uh, go to the store.

410
00:22:40,225 --> 00:22:42,165
I'd fall for a suit.

411
00:22:42,885 --> 00:22:46,365
Oh, what am I gonna tell Dad?

412
00:22:48,825 --> 00:22:52,005
What's the point?

413
00:23:07,585 --> 00:23:08,995
What's this?

414
00:23:11,585 --> 00:23:14,005
Burst panic. The big crash.

415
00:23:15,585 --> 00:23:17,064
Never heard of it.

416
00:23:18,585 --> 00:23:21,030
I kind of figured.

417
00:23:28,285 --> 00:23:32,040
It's set in the Badlands? Is it?

418
00:23:32,245 --> 00:23:33,075
Yep.

419
00:23:33,158 --> 00:23:35,165
It's a nomad flick, after all.

420
00:23:48,825 --> 00:23:51,582
Give me the Lexington.

421
00:23:51,665 --> 00:23:56,122
Never thought I'd use
this pea shooter again.

422
00:23:56,205 --> 00:23:59,322
Takes me back to my rookie days.

423
00:23:59,405 --> 00:24:05,072
To see you.

424
00:24:05,155 --> 00:24:10,135
one last

425
00:24:10,218 --> 00:24:13,282
time.

426
00:24:13,365 --> 00:24:17,210
Oh, Avida?

427
00:24:22,905 --> 00:24:29,905
Avida!

428
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,482
I

429
00:24:45,565 --> 00:24:52,565
don't

430
00:24:57,085 --> 00:25:04,085
know.

431
00:25:13,365 --> 00:25:19,452
We don't

432
00:25:19,535 --> 00:25:23,052
feel

433
00:25:23,135 --> 00:25:29,382
the same.

434
00:25:29,465 --> 00:25:32,122
All I needed was to get it straight.

435
00:25:32,205 --> 00:25:36,385
How I feel, even complicated.

436
00:25:36,805 --> 00:25:41,122
Everything that I longed
to be, you and me.

437
00:25:41,205 --> 00:25:43,702
There's more than meets the eye.

438
00:25:43,785 --> 00:25:46,242
I'm everything I want to be.

439
00:25:46,325 --> 00:25:52,782
I see you and I'm wandering on

440
00:25:52,865 --> 00:25:57,125
the city harbor.

441
00:25:57,585 --> 00:25:58,415
Not

442
00:25:58,498 --> 00:25:59,452
possibly

443
00:25:59,535 --> 00:26:03,432
I will see you and watch

444
00:26:03,515 --> 00:26:07,185
them fall away with me.

445
00:26:07,285 --> 00:26:11,545
You're my West Coast problem.

446
00:26:11,705 --> 00:26:18,525
Now, finally, we are going home.

447
00:26:18,985 --> 00:26:22,822
Once again, I lose it all.

448
00:26:22,905 --> 00:26:27,732
Once again,

449
00:26:27,815 --> 00:26:33,935
I lose it all.

450
00:26:34,165 --> 00:26:39,585
♪ I'm begging for this love
once again, I'll lose it all ♪

451
00:27:05,345 --> 00:27:12,345
Thank

452
00:27:23,295 --> 00:27:30,295
you.

453
00:27:35,345 --> 00:27:42,345
Thank

454
00:27:53,295 --> 00:28:00,295
you.

455
00:28:04,765 --> 00:28:11,765
Thank

456
00:28:15,105 --> 00:28:22,105
you.

